{"connection_id": "BC-38eacd503d6104be4269", "ref": "WLC:Prov.8.20", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking in the midst of paths of justice", "note": "Wisdom says she walks in the way of righteousness, in the midst of paths of justice; the wording offers a concrete counterpart to the commentary’s road-center image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c84b36b318988acca6fa", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.1", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking, standing, and sitting as a settled pattern", "note": "The verse traces a person’s association with wicked counsel from walking to standing to sitting; it gives the commentary’s secondary sense of a route as a gradually settled pattern."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5df71417ec745c13b036", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.1", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessed person does not walk in the wicked's counsel", "note": "The opening beatitude defines a favored walker by refusing the wicked's counsel and way, giving the two paths distinct human company."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cfcb25764fa6666eda42", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.5", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew קום at the judgment", "note": "The commentary labels Arabic ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ with the source root ق و م; Hebrew קום here means to stand, not to be straight. Its use when the wicked cannot stand in judgment makes the cognate’s judgment setting a secondary echo, not an equivalent meaning."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cb039aa893365a131e5b", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.5", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "standing in the righteous congregation at judgment", "note": "The wicked cannot stand in judgment or remain in the congregation of the righteous; this adds the separation of communities at judgment to the contrast of their ways in the neighboring verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-67958fb95a3f80399f35", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.5", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "judgment and assembly of righteous", "note": "The wicked cannot stand in judgment or in the assembly of the righteous, joining Fātiḥa's reckoning day to its differentiated communal destinies."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7e05585fc54052c9a0b0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "two paths and their different ends", "note": "The Lord knows the way of the righteous while the way of the wicked perishes; the verse makes a community’s road a moral course with distinct outcomes."}
{"connection_id": "BC-67bf0d6b3806a337cf6e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.1.6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the LORD knows the righteous way, wicked way perishes", "note": "The final contrast names a way known by God and a way that perishes, providing both divine oversight and a terminal division of routes."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e73e7d0dad30d7dc39b4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.4", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wanderers cannot find a dwelling city", "note": "The travelers lose their way in the wilderness and find no city to live in; this makes the commentary’s image of failing to find both road and home concrete."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a55cbcb7b196f02cf6ff", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.4", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost traveler, missing road and city", "note": "The commentary's traveler cannot find either the route or its home; the psalm's wilderness wanderers likewise find no way to an inhabited city."}
{"connection_id": "BC-46675a6292ca1a296f87", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.7", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads to a city by a straight way", "note": "After wandering, the travelers are led on a straight route to an inhabited city; road, guidance, straightness, and home converge in one verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-532314dbd07dc1bf9d11", "ref": "WLC:Ps.107.7", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "led by a straight way to a city", "note": "The psalm answers the same route-and-destination crisis by saying that God led the wanderers by a straight way until they reached a city to live in."}
{"connection_id": "BC-73ccc6a120cd8e6621f5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.1", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessed people whose way is blameless", "note": "The psalm calls blessed those blameless in way who walk in the LORD's instruction, a concise counterpart to the favored community's path."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2c3b206824d141c9b6a6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.105", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lamp at the feet and light on the path", "note": "The divine word illuminates the traveler’s feet and path, a concrete scriptural image for signs that allow a person to keep direction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-83021bf1c173069ca6fb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.105", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lamp for feet and light for path", "note": "Word as a lamp for feet and a light for a path turns guidance into a visible orientation aid, alongside the commentary's signs that let a traveler find the way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-18460d18088cc3646db9", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.133", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "steps made firm by the divine word", "note": "The speaker asks that his steps be established by God’s word so sin will not rule him; the path is held steady through instruction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9456f4a0ecc891cb86c4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.176", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lost sheep and a search for return", "note": "The speaker calls himself a straying sheep and asks God to seek him; this is a close image of a lost traveler needing the guide to bring him back."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a23194ce96dc3ee4f490", "ref": "WLC:Ps.119.35", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "make me walk in the path of commandments", "note": "The psalmist asks to be made to walk in the path of commandments because he delights in it, preserving both a prayer for guidance and ongoing habitual movement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9cb8350b1332a1c1530d", "ref": "WLC:Ps.122.2", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "feet arrive at the gates of the Lord’s house", "note": "The speaker says their feet are standing inside Jerusalem’s gates after the call to go to the Lord’s house; it gives the route-to-home image a communal pilgrimage and worship setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-491a14f476188212bee0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.140.6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "snares laid beside a path", "note": "The enemies spread nets and snares beside the path, a close physical counterpart to the hostile figure waiting upon and around the straight way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1e175c8e318a3f4f602f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.11", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God teaches and leads on level ground", "note": "The prayer asks God to teach the divine will and lead the speaker on level ground; it joins teaching, guidance, and a straight route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a0c3ee36003c1fd89616", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.11", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "good Spirit leads on level ground", "note": "The prayer asks for the good Spirit to lead the speaker on level ground, directly combining divine guidance with the commentary's flat, passable road."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9f4874870a3fb8a56ff8", "ref": "WLC:Ps.143.9", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the prayer asks to know which way to go", "note": "The speaker asks God to make him know the way he should go; this is nearly the same act of petition as the commentary’s opening request for guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e36e06f743466af939d4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.16.11", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "path of life and its destination", "note": "God makes known the path of life, whose endpoint is joy in God’s presence; this is a specific path-and-destination image without a guide walking ahead."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec18d17684dce08bceec", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.3", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shepherd leads on righteous paths", "note": "The shepherd leads the speaker along paths of righteousness, joining a guide who goes ahead with the communal and ethical road in the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a4d1c8c51b2a616197ef", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.4", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "staff carried through a dangerous valley", "note": "The speaker’s rod and staff comfort him while walking through the valley, a concrete staff-on-the-road image; the verse does not say the staff goes ahead as the commentary’s gloss does."}

{"connection_id": "BC-cc8e7435bfc3083d92aa", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.4", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shepherd leads in paths of righteousness", "note": "The shepherd restores the traveler and leads him in righteous tracks, a direct shepherd-guide form of the requested path."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ad32cae87110c006fe00", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.5", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rod and staff in the dark valley", "note": "The commentary's staff goes ahead as a guide; in this walking-through-danger scene the shepherd's rod and staff comfort the traveler, giving the object a related but not identical role."}
{"connection_id": "BC-72fff48d7266d2ed4b3f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.23.6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "dwelling in the LORD's house", "note": "The psalm's guided traveler ends by dwelling in the LORD's house, supplying the homeward terminus paired with the commentary's route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-008f4314ddd52b9288e8", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.4", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "showing and teaching the paths", "note": "The speaker asks God to make the divine ways known and teach the paths; this is a direct prayer for the commentary’s first movement, having the route shown."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc06ab2b66c309871cfa", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.5", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "being led along the way", "note": "The speaker asks God to lead him in truth; it adds active guidance to the commentary’s request to be taken along a known route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a14517d6427f34b0b6a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.27.12", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teaching and leading on a level path", "note": "The speaker asks God to teach the way and lead him on a level path; the prayer unites instruction with continued movement on course."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cde4948ad446b8eb0be7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.32.9", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "instruction in the way with a guiding eye", "note": "God promises to instruct and teach the way and guide the learner with an eye; this makes guidance personal and ongoing rather than a bare direction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7f3ae16a2456baf157c4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.37.23", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the Lord establishes a person’s steps", "note": "The Lord establishes the steps of the one whose way pleases him; the path is shaped and sustained by divine guidance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2b647501033d64510e9f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.37.24", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the Lord holds the traveler when he stumbles", "note": "Even if the righteous person stumbles, the Lord holds his hand and keeps him from falling; this adds support on the path when the walk falters."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e414a2f093d6b788b025", "ref": "WLC:Ps.43.3", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light leads to the divine dwelling", "note": "The speaker asks for light and truth to lead him to the holy mountain and dwelling; a guiding marker and the road’s destination meet in one prayer."}
{"connection_id": "BC-20a817eefe3de333cd47", "ref": "WLC:Ps.84.6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "highways held in the heart toward Zion", "note": "The pilgrims have highways in their hearts as they go toward God in Zion; the road is the inwardly held route of a worshiping community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bcd2b3e78a0d41b642a4", "ref": "WLC:Ps.84.7", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "pilgrims cross the Baca valley", "note": "The travelers pass through a dry valley that becomes springs; it supplies a concrete terrain on the community’s road to worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-385af745233cf103c06c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.84.8", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the pilgrims arrive before God in Zion", "note": "The group goes from strength to strength until each appears before God in Zion; this completes the journey’s destination rather than leaving the path abstract."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4c82e7f0e0547b1fdb39", "ref": "WLC:Ps.85.14", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteousness goes before and makes a way", "note": "Righteousness goes before God and makes a way from his steps, a poetic image of a preceding presence whose passage establishes the route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17364381c6e00a1c5a4a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.86.11", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "teach me your way so I can walk in truth", "note": "The prayer asks God to teach the way and unite the speaker’s heart to serve God; it joins route instruction to worshipful commitment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a35b5919590b2399396d", "ref": "WLC:Zech.11.7", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נעם in the name of a shepherd’s staff", "note": "The commentary labels Arabic أَنْعَمْتَ with source root ن ع م; Hebrew נֹעַם names a staff and belongs to the related Semitic n-ʿ-m family, though its sense here is pleasantness rather than the verb of bestowing favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9ca023bce991eadac3fa", "ref": "WLC:Zech.11.7", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "staff named Favor in a shepherding scene", "note": "The shepherd tends the flock with two staffs, one named Noam and one named Bonds; this brings a favor-named staff, guidance, and a gathered flock into one concrete scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d4af307a30db9baf6e81", "ref": "Wisdom 10:10", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Wisdom guides on straight paths and shows a kingdom", "note": "Wisdom guides the fleeing righteous person on straight paths and shows him God's kingdom, unusually preserving together the straight route, guide, and disclosed destination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-123b086bfc925dab776c", "ref": "Wisdom 10:17", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Wisdom guides by way, shelter by day, stars by night", "note": "Wisdom guides the holy people along a remarkable way and becomes their shelter by day and starlight by night, unusually gathering guide, road, and celestial orientation signs."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9215be369a6bce9c6343", "ref": "Wisdom 5:6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "straying from truth's way", "note": "The impious confess that they strayed from the way of truth and did not know the Lord's way, directly joining lost direction with a missed moral destination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e9c37313edec31b5a08e", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 5:6", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the speaker says they strayed from truth’s way", "note": "The speakers confess that they left the way of truth and lacked the light of righteousness; the passage connects wrong direction with moral failure and lost illumination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fb33c3fae6674a457f70", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 5:7", "target": "sec1", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lawless travel through trackless deserts", "note": "The speakers say they traveled through trackless deserts without knowing the Lord’s way; this brings astray, pathlessness, and ignorance of the right route together."}

